\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Exact relabelings transport the background data}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{An \vocabk{exact relabeling}{fdip-000G} induces counting isometries
#{P:\mathbb R^V\to\mathbb R^{V'}} and
#{J:\mathbb R^E\to\mathbb R^{E'}}. They preserve the weighted edge
pairing and the reference volumes and satisfy
##{d'P=Jd,\qquad W'J=JW,\qquad
L'=PLP^{-1},\qquad Q'=PQP^{-1}.}
The normalized laws and their moving retained marginals are transported
by #{P} and #{P_R}, respectively. Identity, inverse and composition
of exact relabelings are exact relabelings; existence of one is an
equivalence relation on the specified backgrounds.}

\proof{
\p{Reindexing the counting sums proves that #{P} and #{J} preserve
their pairings. In the weighted sum use #{w'(q(e))=w(e)} as well.
Evaluation at #{q(e)} gives
#{(d'Pf)(q(e))=f(h(e))-f(s(e))=(Jdf)(q(e))}; the same evaluation
gives #{W'J=JW}. This retains the attachment of a loop even when its
incidence is zero. The [paired transport theorem](fdip-003D) gives
the two conjugacies. Counting isometry gives
#{P^\dagger=P^{-1}} and #{J^\dagger=J^{-1}}. In the induced
volumes, [Gaussian transport](fdip-000H) proves volume and law
preservation, including the moving retained target, its full fiber
scalar and its normalized marginal.}
\p{All signs in the [signed endpoint arrows](fdip-003B) are positive.
Their proved identity, inverse and composition laws therefore remain
in this subclass. The background weights, positive mass and retained
subset are preserved by these operations. The identity proves
reflexivity, the inverse proves symmetry, and composition proves
transitivity of existence.}
}
\p{This is the directed specialization of the endpoint and operator
transport results. The group-action convention is
\citet{Definition 4.1, pp. 57-58}{milne2025group}; the normalized
Gaussian substitution uses
\citet{Proposition B.55, p. 505}{friedli2017statistical}.}
